/**
 * Oncology companies from investor and accelerator portfolios that OnCo did not hold, found by the startup monitors
 * (scripts/startup-monitors.ts: the Y Combinator, ARCH, Third Rock, a16z, Khosla, OrbiMed, RA Capital, Atlas and
 * Flagship portfolio queues, listed in the "Startup monitors" section of the freshness issue, #336). A portfolio tile is
 * only a pointer: each company was confirmed on its own website, or, for a company that no longer exists, on its
 * acquirer's release or an SEC filing, read as raw text on 2026-11-04. Companies whose cancer work was incidental, that
 * now work outside cancer, or whose site could not confirm a cancer focus were left out, and so were a veterinary test
 * and a care provider. Acquired and merged companies are recorded under their own names with the acquisition and its
 * source. The founding year appears only where a source states it (a Companies House incorporation date is labelled as
 * such in the notes). The investors named on each record are the portfolio that listed it, plus any investor the
 * company's own releases name. Registered in src/data/index.ts.
 */

